\name{cellucid_camera_path_stop}
\alias{cellucid_camera_path_stop}
\title{Stop the camera path}
\usage{
cellucid_camera_path_stop(viewer)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{stopped} (False when no camera path was playing).
}
\description{
Stop a playing camera path where the camera is, at once, also while camera_path_play is still waiting for it to end (that play then answers ended "stopped", and its step holds the camera where it stopped).
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{camera-path.stop} (Camera path). It stops work under way in the viewer at once, also while the request that started it is still waiting; that work's own step records what it changed: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_camera_path_stop(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
